  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat is the retail price of one pack of glue sticks at the school-supply store? Mr. Jackson’s fourth-grade class has 28 students.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. The class has 28 students, but no information is given about the total cost of the glue sticks or how many packs were purchased.\n2. Therefore, the retail price of one pack cannot be calculated.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Cannot be determined from the information given}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Mr. Jackson’s fourth-grade class has 27 students.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Knowing that Mr. Jackson’s class has 27 students still does not provide the cost or number of glue-stick packs purchased. Therefore, the retail price cannot be determined.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Cannot be determined from the information given}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: the glue sticks come in packs of 9.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "27 students ÷ 9 glue sticks per pack = 3 packs.\n\nHowever, no total cost or price information is provided, so the retail price of one pack cannot be determined.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Cannot be determined from the information given}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. The glue sticks come in packs of 8.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "With 27 students and 8 glue sticks per pack:\n\n\\[\n27 \\div 8 = 3\\text{ remainder }3\n\\]\n\nSo the class would need 4 packs to give every student one glue stick. However, the price of each pack is not provided.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Cannot be determined from the information given}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: the school-supply store sells each pack of glue sticks for $6.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The school-supply store sells each pack for **$6**. The class size and pack size are not needed to determine the price of one pack.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$6}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: the store does not offer discounts on glue-stick packs.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since the store sells each pack for $6 and does not offer discounts, the retail price remains:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$6}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Thanks, that helps. Now I want to figure out: How many packs of glue sticks does Mr. Jackson need to buy so every student can have 2 glue sticks? By the way, here are some relevant details: Mr. Jackson wants to give each student 2 glue sticks. Mr. Jackson can only buy whole packs and expects to have some extra glue sticks left over.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. Mr. Jackson needs \\(27 \\times 2 = 54\\) glue sticks.\n2. Each pack contains 8 glue sticks.\n3. Since he must buy whole packs:\n\n\\[\n54 \\div 8 = 6.75\n\\]\n\nHe must round up to 7 packs. This provides:\n\n\\[\n7 \\times 8 = 56\n\\]\n\nglue sticks, leaving 2 extra.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7\\text{ packs}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
